WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:01.050
Please Be Generous, Your Highness

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.950
What's wrong with you?
Hurry up!

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.910
I know! I know!

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.290
Sorry!

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.630
There's no time to waste!
A true police officer never...

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:37.630
YOU sure took
your time in there!

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:44.140
We're the last ones.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.060
Hurry!
They're just landing!

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:51.690
Wait!

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.750
So that's the Prince of Oasis.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.330
He sure is young.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.090
It's a small country,

00:03:57.090 --> 00:04:02.260
but they have
significant oil reserves.

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:08.930
I thought
he was coming in secret.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.390
Why are they putting
on such a show?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.160
So I'm finally seeing
the model 98 Ingram!

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:32.580
Look at that! It's so charming
and majestic! It's beautiful!

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.960
Hold on!

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:37.670
This is dangerous,
so please stand back.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.510
Do not alarm yourself.
Tell me this:

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.470
That machine has a
non-standard head.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.220
For what purpose?

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:53.980
Oh, that's just Ota's...

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:58.770
Hey! Who are you?

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.860
My question first.
Answer me.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:05.110
Captain!

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:11.160
They got separated from
the Prince's entourage.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.330
Actually, this IS the prince.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.080
The other was a stand-in.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:20.710
Your Highness, welcome
to the Patlabor team!

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.670
I thank you for your
gracious hospitality.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.180
We'd better take
care of your clothes.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:31.010
We dressed him inconspicuously.
Is that a problem?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:40.770
That was the start of my strange
acquaintance with the prince.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.370
- Is this all right?
- What?

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:01.420
Letting an heir to a throne poke
around in dangerous equipment.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:02.500
Let him.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:08.300
Thanks for your help. Why is he
in a Special Vehicles uniform?

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.140
That's why he came to Japan.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.600
His cousin is handling
the dull diplomacy.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:16.850
The prince came to see
a Japanese Labor team,

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:20.100
so he can set one up
in his own country.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.070
He came to observe?
Well, well, well.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.400
What?

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:28.070
Just whom does
that remind you of?

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.320
So you think so, too?

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:31.780
Definitely.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.160
Why are you
looking at me?

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.750
No! I don't do that!

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.710
Conference Room

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:45.800
What's going on?

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:01.190
Does he think he can get away
with this? It'll destroy morale!

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:05.770
Our bunk room
suddenly seems so tiny.

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.190
What are you doing?

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.160
Captain, what is
the meaning of this?

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:17.040
Oh, that. The prince can't
sleep in a strange bed,

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.330
and no other room
is big enough.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:22.580
I couldn't make him
sleep in the hanger!

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.670
But he's supposed to be
treated like everyone else!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:30.470
Well, he just invited us to dinner.
What are you going to do?

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:33.140
Don't expect me
to hide my outrage!

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.730
Then I guess
you don't want any.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:46.770
That was delicious!

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.570
Been a while since
I've had a feed like that!

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.070
I hope this prince
stays a while!

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.070
You sure changed your tune.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.030
I didn't see <i>you</i>
holding back.

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.450
Shinshi, telephone.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:01.250
Thank you.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.830
Hello, Tamiko. No, I can't
come home this week, either.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:10.760
Supper? No, I'm eating fine.
We just had a fabulous feast!

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.380
It was delicious!

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.680
What? No, I don't mean that!

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.350
No, no, Tamiko!

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:22.140
Don't I always say your beef
stew is the best in the world?

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.100
Tamiko! Tamiko!

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.740
How did it go?

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.290
So... where's the prince?

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.290
Isn't he with you?

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.670
He went to the hanger
with Kanuka and Izumi.

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.040
I think I'll check!

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:50.960
I... have to go to
the bathroom!

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.050
Me too!

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.740
I think we're just interfering,
Asuma.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.740
So you want to start a Labor
team in your country?

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:20.410
Yes.

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.120
Do you have a problem
with Labor crime?

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:26.000
No, there aren't any Labors,

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.710
so we certainly don't
have any Labor crime.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.040
Then why...?

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.420
Because I want one.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:37.180
I love Labors,
especially the Ingram.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:43.350
I got so excited when I first
saw its picture in Newsweek.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.980
Great power and strength, in a
frame that's so gentle and kind.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:50.730
I've always wanted
to touch an Ingram.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:56.820
What?

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:58.910
You're not laughing.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:09:59.910
Laughing?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:05.120
Usually when I say that,
people think I'm joking.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:07.660
But you're different.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:12.250
I love Labors, too.
I love Alphonse.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:19.470
It's wonderful to meet
someone who understands.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:23.970
Yeah, well...
Want to see the cockpit?

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.220
Really?
You'll show me?

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:27.310
Sure.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:31.900
It's a little tight in here.

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:36.030
Incredible!
Can you use all of these?

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.570
Of course.
Your Highness, look at this!

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.490
He's JUST a machine-maniac!

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:50.540
You called me?

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.000
I just got back
from headquarters.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.880
This is a West German
type 7 Brocken.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:02.260
It's one of the pair
we seized at Tokyo Teleport.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.100
What's wrong with it?

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:06.390
It's been stolen.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.680
Along with the movement disk.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.440
A professional job?

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:11.900
Looks like it.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:15.520
It was removed from the
warehouse a few days ago,

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:19.950
supposedly for a
late-night cleaning.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:23.620
That's bad news.
So what do we do?

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:28.790
We realized that Captain Goto
is holding a bomb right now.

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:31.120
The prince.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:34.330
Do you think this is related
to his arrival in Japan?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.300
They won't be able to
hide a Brocken for long.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:44.090
Before they move, let's put
the next few days to good use.

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.510
- Which means?
- We think it IS related.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:52.480
And if it is, they can't do much
while he's here.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.400
I hope you're right.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.370
Special Carrier

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.090
What's this?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:20.340
It's my breakfast.

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:22.130
You merely add hot water?

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:23.260
Right.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.520
Bring me some of this.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:34.730
Yes, Your Highness. I shall
acquire some immediately.

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:36.440
And don't forget the caviar.

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:40.230
Caviar?

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:46.740
Are you sure this is okay?

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:48.660
The captain agreed.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.450
- That's not what I mean.
- What?

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:54.710
You wouldn't use a Porsche or
Ferrari in a Driver's Ed school.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.210
They might in his country.

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.090
So this is what it's
like to be a pilot!

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.090
Noa, instruct me!

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:08.050
Oh, "instruct me!"

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.680
Asuma, he'll hear you!

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:12.220
Your Highness,
have you checked the meters?

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.140
Don't worry, they're green.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.560
Okay then, try walking.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.060
Splendid.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.320
That's too big a step!

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.860
What a joke!

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.320
Asuma, watch out!

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:41.090
I shall always remember this
as a great step forward!

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:46.130
Here I go!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.930
Hey, this is easy!

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:59.060
Shige, call Unit 2 off standby.
We'll need more help for this job.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:02.860
Wow, he's really putting the
Ingram through its paces!

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:05.360
We mechanics have
our work cut out for us!

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.570
I'm going to cry.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.660
Thank you for waiting.
Round two of lunch:

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.460
Today's lunch is... THIS!

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:29.050
In my country,
food preservation is essential.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:33.810
I was stunned to learn you can
make food just by adding water!

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:37.060
There are so many things
that I don't yet know!

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:40.850
We have to wait three minutes!

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:42.980
What a long time!

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:48.650
I hope to try all the varieties
before I leave Japan.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:52.120
This is the first time you've
ever heard of Cup Ramen?

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:53.280
Correct.

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:57.870
A Brocken has
appeared in area 102B-9.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.460
Division 2, mobilize
immediately. I repeat...

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:11.720
Answer me:
Where is area 102B-9?

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:14.470
Shibuya,
if you know where that is.

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:16.010
I understand.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:19.600
I will accompany you.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:23.020
No, we can't bring you along.
You have to stay here.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.310
I thought
I was a team member.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.530
Then you have to follow
your captain's orders.

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:32.110
My stand-in is at the
broadcasting center today.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:35.160
Isn't that where the
Brocken appeared?

00:15:35.370 --> 00:15:36.740
Yes.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.620
I'm descended from Karimahn!

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:42.620
Karimahn?

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:46.590
A great desert hero, who placed
his fate in the hands of Allah.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:50.510
My cousin is doubling for me.
It's my fault he's in danger!

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:53.590
I can't cower in safety
while his life is at risk!

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.100
You'll follow my orders
when we reach the scene.

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:02.890
Get my clothing.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:31.670
Shinshi and Yamazaki,
close off the west and south gates.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.800
I'll tighten the noose!

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:40.180
He's dangerous.
Don't get careless.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.020
I can handle it!

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:45.690
Halt!

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:51.440
- Damn!
- Well? Go after him!

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.410
Noa, be careful!

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.320
- Follow him!
- Roger!

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.880
The prince at the
studio is a double.

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:10.000
Kill the real one.
Distract the Ingrams.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:16.300
Your Highness!

00:17:19.260 --> 00:17:22.470
Izumi, the prince is headed
your way. Protect him!

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:23.730
Roger.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:42.700
Stay back!

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:51.380
Your Highness!

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.260
You'll have to get
through me, first!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:08.600
Where's the prince?

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:10.560
- He's with me.
- What?

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:12.610
They were shooting at him.

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:14.780
I'm fine.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:15.650
Here he comes.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:20.990
Why you!

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.080
- Don't retreat!
- But...

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.540
You handle the legs.
Advance!

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.550
Trust me.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.520
Let's go!

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.900
Let's go!

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.450
I did it!

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:03.990
Your punch jammed
the finger joints!

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:24.350
Why you!

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:12.390
Captain, put a dragnet
around the park.

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:13.980
We can still
catch the sniper.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.150
We just picked him up.

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:37.750
What happened
in that cockpit?

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:40.670
- What do you mean?
- Well, uh...

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.470
It was perfect!

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.810
I delivered the killing blow!

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:52.060
What are you thinking?

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:57.400
I'm just glad that
you're both safe.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:58.770
Weirdo.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.610
Thank you for your hospitality
these past few days.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:12.080
The sniper and the Brocken pilot
were both from your country.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:13.910
They were professional assassins.

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:17.500
Regretfully, I must rush home.

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:21.050
I must protect my father and
family from these usurpers.

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:26.840
This is a present from Sakaki,
Shige, and the mechanics.

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:30.350
Is this...?

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.810
It's a copy of Alphonse's
movement disk.

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:38.690
Really? You mean I can come back
and pilot him again?

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:39.860
Thank you!

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:44.360
And, Your Highness, this is
from everyone in Division 2!

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.360
Thank you!

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:52.830
Good luck.

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:58.750
Thank you for everything!

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.430
Goodbye, Alphonse.

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:20.940
He's rather naive,
but he is a good prince.

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:25.110
Too bad he's about to get
tied up in all that internal strife.

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:28.030
You should be more
respectful of him.

00:22:28.450 --> 00:22:30.910
Yeah, after all,
he's a great desert hero.

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:34.620
Thank goodness
we're just commoners.

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:45.340
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:49.050
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:55.310
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:02.730 --> 00:23:04.820
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:04.940 --> 00:23:07.740
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:12.320
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:16.990
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:19.830
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:24.000
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:30.510
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.760
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:38.310
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:41.520
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:45.610
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:47.980 --> 00:23:51.780
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:57.830
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:04.460
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:09.710
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:09.710
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:14.390 --> 00:24:16.050
Oh, brother, what a mess!

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:20.270
Ota and Shinohara injure themselves
during a departmental Judo tournament.

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:24.020
Captain, what happens
if we get called to mobilize?

00:24:24.020 --> 00:24:26.730
No deployment...
just kidding.

00:24:26.810 --> 00:24:29.730
Oh well, I'll have to put you
under Kanuka's command.

00:24:29.730 --> 00:24:32.280
Yikes! Oh, Captain,
you can't be serious!

00:24:32.900 --> 00:24:36.910
Next time, "You Win!"
Target locked on!

00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:41.330
Next episode

00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:41.330
You Win!
